ey":"map/bz1h","title":"Slave pen","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz2h","title":"Suslanger and its surroundings","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz4h","title":"Wormface cave","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/bz4h","title":"Wormface temple","variant":""}],"title":"Locations"}],"versions":[{"guide":"","html":"<article><h1>Suslanger</h1><h2>Setting</h2><p>Suslanger is a small, arid possession of Khadagan. Irrigation supports its farms, while harsh and corrupt authority coexists with criminal networks, smuggling and blackmail. Kir and Kel meet in its slave pen. Their escape leads through estates, thieves’ contacts, the Last Shelter and the search for information about the Joons before military papers provide a way to Gipath. [1, 2, 3, 4]</p><h2>Sources</h2><p>Based on the original game dialogue and world descriptions. Source numbers refer to the scenes listed below.</p><table data-columns=\"2\"><tr><th>#</th><th>Sources</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>World description · Suslanger (allod suslanger)</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/merc2\">Kel</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a> (briefing brief_2)</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/merc10\">Aliya</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/glav\">Brother Khatul</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a> (briefing brief_41)</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/sergant\">Sergeant Zairak</a> (briefing brief_88a)</td></tr></table><h2>Inhabitants</h2><table data-columns=\"1\"><tr><th>Related page</th></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/merc10\">Aliya</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/guru\">Brainripper</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/glav\">Brother Khatul</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/zaku\">Brother Smith</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/merc8\">Feiruz</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/skelet\">Fortu